<title>JAPAN: TSE plans to start large-lot deals in after-hours.</title>
<headline>TSE plans to start large-lot deals in after-hours.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Tokyo Stock Exchange (TSE) said on Monday it plans to start trade of large-lot stocks after the regular trade session ends from as early as April 1998, in view of the nation's Big Bang financial reforms.  </p>
<p>The bourse plans to set up on-line trading systems, ToSNeT-1 and -2, on which institutional investors can conduct large-lot cross-trading, basket trading and other deals.</p>
